   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve given by \\( xy^{2} - x^{3} = 10 \\), along which \\( y \\) is a differentiable function of \\( x \\) near the point \\( (2, 3) \\). Find the value of \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} \\) at the point \\( (2, 3) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         35,
         48
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( xy^{2} - x^{3} = 10 \\) implicitly with respect to \\( x \\): \\( - 3 x^{2} + y^{2} + \\left(2 x y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\), so \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{3 x}{2 y} - \\frac{y}{2 x} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Divide",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  3,
                  "x"
               ],
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "y"
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  "y",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{3 x^{2} - y^{2}}{2 x y} \\) again with the quotient rule, treating \\( y \\) as a function of \\( x \\): \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{2 x y \\left(- 2 \\frac{dy}{dx} y + 6 x\\right) - \\left(3 x^{2} - y^{2}\\right) \\left(2 \\frac{dy}{dx} x + 2 y\\right)}{4 x^{2} y^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (2, 3) \\), \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{1}{4} \\). Substitute this value and the coordinates into the second derivative.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            35,
            48
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{35}{48} \\) at \\( (2, 3) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            35,
            48
         ]
      }
